# Frontend Rules

- Vanilla JavaScript only — no React, Vue, or TypeScript.
- Fetch data through `js/api.js`; never read `retro-api/data/` from the browser.
- Use semantic HTML (`main`, `nav`, `button`, `label` + `for`).
- Show user-visible errors when API calls fail; do not fail silently.
- Preserve teaching-oriented simplicity — no new framework without approval.
- Match existing CSS class patterns in `css/` before adding one-off styles.
